      "title": "AN322: Religion, Ritual and Magic (Winter 2027)",
      "description": "AN322: Religion, Ritual and Magic (Winter 2027) Job Details | Wilfrid Laurier University Skip to main content Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Page About Us Why Join Our Team How to apply Career Opportunities Academic Positions Staff and Management Positions View All Positions Join Talent Community Sign Into My Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: AN322: Religion, Ritual and Magic (Winter 2027) Apply now » Date: Aug 26, 2026 Location: Waterloo, CA Company: Wilfrid Laurier University Faculty/Academic Area: Faculty of Arts Department : Anthropology Campus: Waterloo Employee Group: WLUFA Requisition ID: 11733 Position Title: AN322: Religion, Ritual and Magic (Winter 2027) Term: Winter term (January 1 -April 30, 2027) Days/Times: Tuesday and Thursdays, 8:30am-9:50am Hours per week/Hours Total: 3/36 Mode of Delivery: In-Person Type of Instruction: Lecture Anticipated Class Size: 50 Additional Course Requirements: Posted on: July 28, 2026 Posting ends: Sept 4, 2026 AI tools will be used in the hiring process: No Position Summary: The study of ritual performances which relate society to the divine, with a focus on the collective production of meaning. Topics may include: rites of passage, spirit possession, magical beliefs, and the social and epistemological dimensions of religious systems. Qualifications – Required Academic Degree: PhD Qualifications – Required Discipline: Sociocultural Anthropology Qualifications – Required Areas of Specialization: Religion, culture or folklore Salary: $10212.40 (Step 0) Application Deadline: Sept 4, 2026 Submit with Application: Required for All Applicants CV (required) Candidate Application Form (CAF) Teaching Dossier